From 68068219eaa1606f24f162b4781043ff185e14d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheCryptoDonkey <TheCryptoDonkey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:29:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat: pair linked signers from a nostrconnect:// link

identity.link-nostrconnect-start takes { name, purpose?, relays } (one
to 8 relays) and returns { pairing_id, uri }: a nostrconnect:// link
with a fresh client key, a random secret drawn through the entropy
guard, the relays, name=Archipelago and the permissions Archipelago
uses. A spawned listener waits on those relays for the signer's connect
response carrying the secret; responses with any other secret are
ignored, since anyone can publish to the relay. The response author is
the remote signer. The listener then runs the same key proof and
duplicate checks as bunker:// linking and creates the identity with no
stored secret; later sessions reuse the client key.

identity.link-nostrconnect-finish takes { pairing_id } and waits at most
10 s: { status: "pending" } while the signer has not answered or the
proof is still running, { status: "linked", identity } once done, and
an error for a failed, expired or unknown pairing. The signer has 5
minutes to answer; a proof already under way then runs to completion.
A settled pairing repeats its outcome to every poll for a minute, and
at most 4 unsettled pairings run at once.

Both methods follow the dashboard-only origin rule and are rate-limited.
